@startuml
title SokoHub Authorization — Policy-Based Access Control (PBAC)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

[Customer\n(Frontend\nNuxt 3)] as Frontend
package "SokoHub.Api" {
  [SecurityHeadersMiddleware\n(XSS, CSP, HSTS)] as Headers
  [ExceptionHandlingMiddleware\nno stack traces] as Exc
  [HttpsRedirection\n(HTTPS only)] as Https
  [Routing] as Routing
  [AuthenticationMiddleware\n(JWT Bearer validation)] as AuthN
  [AuthorizationMiddleware\n(policy evaluation)] as AuthZ
  [CORS\n(SokoHubPolicy)] as Cors
  [RateLimitMiddleware\n(Redis RateLimitStore)] as Rate
  node "Controller\n(authorize attribute)" as Ctrl
}

package "Identity Domain\n(SokoHub.Domain)" {
  [User\nroleIds[] status\nlockout] as User
  [Role\npermissionIds[]] as Role
  [Permission\n(name)] as Permission
  [UserStatus\nenum:\nPendingVerification|Active\n|Locked|Disabled] as Status
}

database "MSSQL\nUsers/Roles/Permissions" as Db
node "DarajaIpAllowlistMiddleware\n(Safaricom CIDR)" as IpAllow

Frontend --> Https
Https --> Routing
Routing --> AuthN
AuthN --> AuthZ
AuthZ --> Cors
AuthZ --> Rate
Cors --> Ctrl
Rate --> Ctrl

Ctrl --> User : resolve\nICurrentUser\n(Id, RoleIds,\nIsAdmin, IsVendor, IsCustomer)
User --> Role : RoleIds
Role --> Permission : PermissionIds
User --> Status : evaluate\nstatus == Active

note right of AuthN
  Validates JWT signature (HMAC-SHA256)
  Verifies expiry, issuer, audience
  Populates User.Roles claims
  Rejects expired / revoked refresh tokens
end note

note right of AuthZ
  Built-in policies:
    - AdminOnly  (IsAdmin / role = Admin)
    - VendorOnly (IsVendor)
    - CustomerOnly (IsCustomer)
    - RequireAuthenticated
  Fallback: [Authorize] = authenticated user
end note

package "Policy Enforcement Points\n(Controller actions)" {
  [POST /refund\nAdminOnly] as Refund
  [POST /mpesa/callback\nAllowAnonymous] as Callback
  [POST /me\nAuthorize] as Me
}

Ctrl ..> Refund
Ctrl ..> Callback
Ctrl ..> Me

Refund --> AuthZ : AdminOnly\n=> IsAdmin claim\ncheck DB Role/Permission
Me --> AuthZ : RequireAuthenticated\n=> token valid
Callback --> IpAllow : (separate trust\nboundary — see\nmpesa-callback-security.puml)

legend right
  |<b>Trust Boundary</b>||
  |Frontend|Internet|
  |Api|Perimeter|
  |Identity Domain|Platform|
  |Db|Data|
endlegend

@enduml
